  "narrative": [
    "Lower-division requirements seventy-one or seventy-two units total; upper-division requirements forty-eight units total.",
    "\"All courses required and used toward any biology major requirements must be taken for a letter grade of C- or better.\" Exceptions only for P/NP-only courses (BISP 193, 195P, 196, 197, and 199).",
    "\"The minimum GPA requirement (for both the major and overall UC) for graduation is 2.0.\"",
    "Residency: \"all students, including transfer students, must complete at least forty-eight or more units of upper-division course work within the major\" and \"at least twenty units of upper-division course work in the School of Biological Sciences with a grade of C- or better\" while enrolled at UC San Diego.",
    "Satisfactory progress: if the GPA in biology courses falls below 2.0 the student is placed on probation and may be dropped from the major.",
    "Special studies: \"One quarter of BISP 195P may apply as an upper-division elective\"; \"One quarter of BISP 193, 196, 197, or 199 may count toward the upper-division elective requirement\"; 194 Advanced Topics courses may apply to major electives if topics differ and taken for a letter grade of C- or better.",
    "\"Course work taken outside of the School of Biological Sciences may be applicable toward the major, assuming the course has been previously reviewed and approved and meets minimum criteria. Nonreviewed course work must be petitioned.\""
  ],
